{"$schema":"https://json.schemastore.org/sarif-2.1.0.json","runs":[{"artifacts":[{"contents":{"text":"<scxml xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2005/07/scxml\" version=\"1.0\" initial=\"o\">\n  <state id=\"o\">\n    <transition event=\"go\" target=\"h b1\"/>\n    <transition event=\"out\" target=\"o\"/>\n  </state>\n  <parallel id=\"p\">\n    <history id=\"h\"><transition target=\"a\"/></history>\n    <state id=\"a\"><state id=\"a1\"/></state>\n    <state id=\"b\"><state id=\"b0\"/><state id=\"b1\"/></state>\n    <transition event=\"out\" target=\"o\"/>\n  </parallel>\n</scxml>\n"},"location":{"uri":"tests/ui/scxml080-history-and-region-target.scx"},"mimeType":"application/scxml+xml"}],"columnKind":"utf16CodeUnits","properties":{"diagnosticCounts":{"errors":0,"notes":0,"total":2,"warnings":2},"producer":{"kind":"validator"}},"results":[{"level":"warning","locations":[{"physicalLocation":{"artifactLocation":{"uri":"tests/ui/scxml080-history-and-region-target.scx"},"region":{"endColumn":40,"endLine":3,"startColumn":38,"startLine":3}}}],"message":{"markdown":"transition targets `h` and `b1` can place the machine in an illegal configuration\n\n**Note:** entering the history `h` enters its recorded (or default) configuration of `p` (SCXML 1.0 §3.10.2: \"the SCXML processor MUST behave as if the transition had taken the stored state configuration for that history state as its target\"); unless that configuration contains `b1`, the machine ends up with two active children of one state, and \"A conformant SCXML document MUST place the state machine only in legal state configurations\" (§3.11)\n\n**Help:** target either the history `h` or `b1`, not both\n\n**Spec:** SCXML 1.0 §3.10 <history>\n\n**Spec:** SCXML 1.0 §3.11 Legal State Configurations and Specifications","text":"transition targets `h` and `b1` can place the machine in an illegal configuration"},"properties":{"byteSpan":{"end":130,"start":128},"category":"lint"},"relatedLocations":[{"id":1,"message":{"text":"`h` is entered here"},"physicalLocation":{"artifactLocation":{"uri":"tests/ui/scxml080-history-and-region-target.scx"},"region":{"endColumn":37,"endLine":3,"startColumn":36,"startLine":3}}}],"ruleId":"SCXML080"},{"fixes":[{"artifactChanges":[{"artifactLocation":{"uri":"tests/ui/scxml080-history-and-region-target.scx"},"replacements":[{"deletedRegion":{"byteLength":0,"byteOffset":321,"endColumn":18,"endLine":9,"startColumn":18,"startLine":9},"insertedContent":{"text":" initial=\"b0\""}}]}],"description":{"text":"make the current entry state `b0` explicit"},"properties":{"applicability":"machine-applicable"}}],"level":"warning","locations":[{"physicalLocation":{"artifactLocation":{"uri":"tests/ui/scxml080-history-and-region-target.scx"},"region":{"endColumn":11,"endLine":9,"startColumn":6,"startLine":9}}}],"message":{"markdown":"compound state `b` has several child states but no explicit initial state\n\n**Note:** without `initial`, the first of several child states in document order is entered; reordering children silently changes behavior (a single child state is not reported)\n\n**Help:** make the entry explicit with `initial=\"b0\"` (keeps the current behavior), or name the state that should be entered first\n\n**Spec:** SCXML 1.0 §3.3 <state>","text":"compound state `b` has several child states but no explicit initial state"},"properties":{"byteSpan":{"end":314,"start":309},"category":"lint"},"relatedLocations":[{"id":1,"message":{"text":"entered first because it comes first in document order"},"physicalLocation":{"artifactLocation":{"uri":"tests/ui/scxml080-history-and-region-target.scx"},"region":{"endColumn":32,"endLine":9,"startColumn":30,"startLine":9}}}],"ruleId":"LINT001"}],"tool":{"driver":{"informationUri":"https://www.w3.org/TR/scxml/","name":"scxml-validator","rules":[{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"warning"},"fullDescription":{"text":"without `initial`, the first of several child states in document order is entered; reordering children silently changes behavior (a single child state is not reported)"},"help":{"text":"How to fix: add an `initial` attribute (or an `<initial>` child) naming the intended first child.\n\nSpecification: SCXML 1.0 §3.3 <state>\n\nRun `scx --explain LINT001` for examples."},"helpUri":"https://www.w3.org/TR/scxml/#state","id":"LINT001","name":"LINT001","properties":{"category":"lint"},"shortDescription":{"text":"a compound state relies on document order for its initial child"}},{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"warning"},"fullDescription":{"text":"SCXML 1.0 §3.10.2: when a transition targets a history pseudo-state, \"the SCXML processor MUST behave as if the transition had taken the stored state configuration for that history state as its target\" (or the default one), which covers the history's parent. Another target inside that parent is legal only when the restored configuration happens to contain it; otherwise the machine gets two active children of one state, and §3.11 says \"A conformant SCXML document MUST place the state machine only in legal state configurations\" (§A.2: a processor's behavior on a non-conformant document is undefined). The recorded configuration is known only at run time, so this is a warning"},"help":{"text":"How to fix: target either the history or the state inside its parent, not both.\n\nSpecification: SCXML 1.0 §3.11 Legal State Configurations and Specifications\n\nRun `scx --explain SCXML080` for examples."},"helpUri":"https://www.w3.org/TR/scxml/#LegalStateConfigurations","id":"SCXML080","name":"SCXML080","properties":{"category":"semantic"},"shortDescription":{"text":"a target set combines a `<history>` with a state it restores"}}],"semanticVersion":"0.2.0"}}}],"version":"2.1.0"}